OL,3,GNEWSANurse opts for 'whole shebang' of
OL,4,Acancer treatment
OL,5,
OL,6,FAfter being a nurse for 24 years Susan
OL,7,FRoyse said she has opted "for the whole
OL,8,Fshebang" of treatment following her
OL,9,Fbreast cancer diagnosis in April.
OL,11,FThe 46-year-old from Harpole,
OL,12,FNorthamptonshire, said she found a lump
OL,13,Fon her left breast that "was tiny to
OL,14,Fbegin with" at the beginning of the
OL,15,Fyear.
OL,17,FThe cardiology specialist nurse said
OL,18,Fshe first thought the lump was down to
OL,19,Fhormone changes, but when it got bigger
OL,20,Fand more painful she visited her GP and
OL,21,Fwas "referred instantly".
OL,23,APub: 24-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
